{title: 143 - Silent Night, Holy Night}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #143 • STILLE NACHT • 6.6.8.9.6.6}
{lyricist: Joseph Mohr}
{composer: Franz Gruber}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 143}
{meta: tune STILLE NACHT}
{meta: meter 6.6.8.9.6.6}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb/F]Silent night, holy night;
[Bb/F]All is calm, all [Adim]is [F]bright
[Bb/F]Round yon [Eb/Bb]virgin [Gm]mother [Bb]and Child,
[Eb/Bb]Holy [Gm]Infant so [Bb]tender and mild,
[Adim]Sleep [F7]in [Bb/F]heavenly [Cm]peace,
[Gm/D]Sleep in heavenly peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb/F]Silent night! holy night!
[Bb/F]Shepherds quake at [Adim]the [F]sight,
[Bb/F]glories [Eb/Bb]stream [Gm]from heaven [Bb]afar,
[Eb/Bb]heavenly [Gm]hosts [Bb]sing Alleluia;
[Adim]Christ, [F7]the [Bb/F]Savior is [Cm]born,
[Gm/D]Christ, the Savior is born.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb/F]Silent night! holy night!
[Bb/F]Son of God, love's [Adim]pure [F]light,
[Bb/F]Radiant [Eb/Bb]beams [Gm]from Thy holy [Bb]face,
[Eb/Bb]with [Gm]the dawn of [Bb]redeeming grace,
[Adim]Jesus, [Bb/F]Lord, at Thy [Cm]birth,
[Gm/D]Jesus, Lord, at Thy birth.
{end_of_verse}
